      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, but it just feels like one side is actually looking forward to bettering the future and the other is just making excuses to keep things the way they are. When you look at the actual arguments, doesn't it seem like the \"pro-choice\" side has a much more logical and forward-thinking foundation for helping individual students, while the opposition is just relying on fear-mongering about budget cuts? Which side actually has the stronger moral ground here?",
